  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "DeNooyer grew up around the family motor trade, working summer jobs at the Albany dealership before studying automotive management at Northwood University and completing the NADA dealer-candidate programme. He returned as a sales manager, moved into the Chevrolet operation and assumed leadership when his father retired in 2000.\n\nUnder DeNooyer, the dealership developed into a high-volume regional business spanning new and used vehicles, servicing and commercial fleets. He told an industry interviewer that the operation had grown to roughly three times its previous size, while maintaining multigenerational family involvement. Repeated Dealer of the Year recognition reflected performance in sales, service and customer satisfaction, and DeNooyer also backed a campaign intended to provide one million meals for local families.",
